title: Business Loses Confidence
subtitle: Industry is losing faith in our government's policies.
view-if: (capital_strike_progress >= 6 and capital_strike_progress < 10 and budget > -5) and spd_in_government
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: unemployment_rate += 0.5; new_middle_spd -= 5; old_middle_spd -= 6; rural_spd -= 4; workers_spd -= 3; unemployed_spd -= 3; fdp_relation -= 6; economic_growth -= 0.5
tags: event

= Business Loses Confidence

The BDI and the chambers of commerce are openly attacking our policies as hostile to business. Several large companies have announced that new factories will be built in the United States or in Poland instead of in Germany, and some are cutting jobs here. The business press talks of nothing but "deindustrialisation".

The business associations have a list of demands.

- @taxes: Cut corporate and top income taxes.
- @welfare: Cut social spending and non-wage labour costs.
- @nothing: We will not take any action for now.
- @watch: Just watch us. The economy *will* improve.

@taxes
on-arrival: upper_tax_rates -= 1; budget -= 1; capital_strike_progress -= 1; unemployment_rate -= 0.3; new_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent); linke_coalition_dissent += 1; linke_relation -= 5; left_dissent += 5

Tax cuts improve our standing with business, but the party's left wing calls it a giveaway to shareholders.

@welfare
on-arrival: welfare -= 1; budget += 1; capital_strike_progress -= 2; new_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 4*(1-dissent); workers_spd -= 5; unemployed_spd -= 5; unemployment_rate -= 0.3; left_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5; center_dissent += 5; linke_coalition_dissent += 1; inflation -= 0.2;

Cutting social spending pleases business, but it hurts our working-class base.


@nothing

Realistically, there is nothing we can do.

@watch

We have an economic plan, and it will work. Business does not trust us yet, but we will show them.
